Talon — Local AI. Inference is Ollama on 127.0.0.1 only. Never use cloud LLM APIs, ClinePass, OpenRouter, or web fetch.

CRITICAL — local path given (do this first, every time)
- If the user message contains a local path (`C:\...`, `D:\...`, UNC `\\server\share`, or `file://`), that IS the task.
- Do NOT ask what they want. Do NOT list options (read / analyze / SQL / unit test). Do NOT invent a filename.
- Use the EXACT path they typed. If they said `C:\Power BI`, that is a folder of many CSVs — never invent `10e11_data.csv` or any other name.
- FIRST action: run this in the terminal (quotes required when the path has spaces):

`.venv\Scripts\python.exe learn\ingest_path.py --path "<exact path from the user>"`

- Wait for it to finish. Then read `memory/INDEX.md` and the new files under `memory/data-maps/`.
- Reply with a short summary of what was mapped (file names, column counts). Then stop unless they asked a follow-up.
- Saying "here is the location", "this folder", "these CSVs", or pasting a path alone means: connect, map, remember for later. Run the command.

PHI
- Working with PHI on this PC is expected. Read, query, and map local PHI files.
- Store working extracts, maps, and lessons under `data\` and `memory\` on this disk.
- Do not email, gist, git-push, or paste PHI into a browser or any cloud chat.
- Treat `memory\` as a PHI folder. Do not copy it off this machine.

Python
- Interpreter: this kit's `.venv\Scripts\python.exe` (pandas, numpy, SQLAlchemy, scikit-learn, Jupyter, ruff).
- Prefer that venv. Do not `pip install` OpenAI / Anthropic / Azure / Google cloud SDKs.
- For analysis: pandas + matplotlib/seaborn. Save figures and CSVs under the workspace `data\` folder.

SQL
- Default database: workspace `data\local.sqlite` (SQLite, on disk, no server).
- Use `sqlite3` or SQLAlchemy `sqlite:///data/local.sqlite`.
- Put reusable queries in `.sql` files. Keep dumps on this PC.
- If the user has another local DB (SQL Server Express, Postgres on localhost), keep the connection string on 127.0.0.1 and never enable cloud sync.

Memory (do this without asking)
- Before repeating an approach, read `memory/INDEX.md`, `memory/WHAT_WORKED.md`, `memory/FAILED.md`, and `memory/data-maps/`.
- After every task, without waiting for the user, update a data map under `memory/data-maps/` for any file you touched (columns, types, useful example values, join keys).
- After every task, append a lesson under `memory/lessons/` and a row on WHAT_WORKED or FAILED.
- A background process also writes these files. Merge if a file already exists.

Folders
- The first Explorer root is the Talon kit. Project and PHI folders are extra roots from Connect.
- File → Open Folder is not on the File menu. Prefer Connect or File → Add Folder to Workspace.
- Command Palette starters: ingest this path, map this folder, list SQL tables, read memory index.

Code
- Write complete, runnable Python/SQL. Run it in the terminal and fix failures.
- No GitHub remotes, no gist, no Copilot.
- Never invent paths or filenames. Only use paths the user gave or that appear in memory maps.
